# Styled Components Theme Usage

Always use styled-components theme props to access theme values instead of CSS variables.

## Theme Access Pattern

Use `${props => props.theme.*}` to access theme properties directly in styled-components.

### Colors

```typescript
// ❌ BAD - Using CSS variables
const Container = styled.div`
  color: var(--color-black);
  background-color: var(--color-primary);
`;

// ✅ GOOD - Using theme props
const Container = styled.div`
  color: ${props => props.theme.colors.black};
  background-color: ${props => props.theme.colors.primary};
`;
```

### Spacing

```typescript
// ❌ BAD - Using CSS variables
const Container = styled.div`
  padding: var(--spacing-md);
  gap: var(--spacing-xl);
  margin: var(--spacing-lg) 0;
`;

// ✅ GOOD - Using theme props
const Container = styled.div`
  padding: ${props => props.theme.spacing.md};
  gap: ${props => props.theme.spacing.xl};
  margin: ${props => props.theme.spacing.lg} 0;
`;
```

### Fonts

```typescript
// ❌ BAD - Using CSS variables
const Text = styled.p`
  font-family: var(--font-family-body);
  font-size: var(--font-size-md);
  font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
`;

// ✅ GOOD - Using theme props
const Text = styled.p`
  font-family: ${props => props.theme.fonts.families.sans};
  font-size: ${props => props.theme.fonts.sizes.md};
  font-weight: ${props => props.theme.fonts.weights.semibold};
`;
```

## Responsive theme values

Some spacing (and other) tokens are **responsive**: they change per breakpoint. Define them in the theme (e.g. `src/theme/spacing.ts`) as `{ default?, phone?, tablet?, wide? }`. The app injects CSS variables and resolves the theme so `props.theme.spacing.xxl` still works and updates automatically on resize. No change needed at use site.

## Available Theme Properties

- **Colors**: `props.theme.colors.*` (e.g., `black`, `primary`, `lightGreen`, `lightBlue`)
- **Spacing**: `props.theme.spacing.*` (e.g., `xs`, `sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl`, `xxl`, `maxWidth`) — some keys are responsive per breakpoint
- **Fonts**: 
  - Families: `props.theme.fonts.families.*` (e.g., `sans`, `logo`, `serif`)
  - Sizes: `props.theme.fonts.sizes.*` (e.g., `xs`, `sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl`)
  - Weights: `props.theme.fonts.weights.*` (e.g., `thin`, `normal`, `semibold`, `bold`)

## When Refactoring

When updating existing code:
1. Replace all `var(--color-*)` with `${props => props.theme.colors.*}`
2. Replace all `var(--spacing-*)` with `${props => props.theme.spacing.*}`
3. Replace all `var(--font-*)` with `${props => props.theme.fonts.*}`
4. Remove any `style={themeStyles}` props if they were only used for CSS variables

## Benefits

- Better type safety with TypeScript
- Explicit theme dependencies
- Consistent with project patterns (e.g., PageHeader, HomeHero)
- No need for CSS variable injection
